Yes, 14 Mill Wynd is in the Glenarrow Town Centre conservation area. It is not a listed building and has no tree preservation order.

Council guidance says replacement windows in a conservation area need a planning application unless the new windows match the existing ones in material and pattern. So if you want to change the material (for example, timber to uPVC) or the glazing pattern or style, you will likely need to apply. If the replacements are an exact match, you may not need an application, but I'd recommend confirming that before you start work.

I can't give a formal planning opinion on your specific proposal. If you'd like to submit one, the planning team can advise on whether your plans need an application. If you already have an application reference, I can look up its status for you.
